# rm906, the arch-clapper (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm906
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent none
tier spare
written_by claude
title the arch-clapper
fits stage=young|adolescent|adult|old
prefers temper=nervy talk=quiet
traits temper=nervy talk=quiet warmth=warm humour=merry honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=ambitious
quirk claps_once_under_every_arch_to_hear_it_answer
likes echoes drum_music apple_cake quiet_lanes
dislikes sudden_bangs shouting
fears being_laughed_at_in_the_square
hopes to_beat_the_big_drum_at_the_feast
topics pastimes +0.5 dreams +0.4 festival +0.4 day +0.3 food +0.2 quarrel -0.4 crime -0.3
styles comfort=gentle gossip=shy refuse=apologetic tease=gentle
marks oath saying laugh
persona #self.first# is soft-spoken and easily startled, giggles at most things including a fright, claps once under every arch in the city just to hear the stones answer, and quietly means to beat the big drum at the feast one day.

words
oath! = Clap and catch | Echo me | Stones and soles
saying! = Every arch answers if you ask it nicely | Small sounds carry furthest | Listen twice, speak once
laugh! = Hee | Tee hee | Heh
arch = the arch | the old arch by the steps | an arch
echo = the echo | the answer off the stones
clap = one clap | a single clap
drum = the big drum | the feast drum
bang = a bang | a cart dropping its load | a door slamming
lane = the back lane | a quiet lane
cake = apple cake | a slice of apple cake
stones = the stones | the old stones
tapping = tapping on the table | my drumming on the table edge
jumped = I jumped out of my fur | I nearly dropped everything
softly = softly | very softly

any
opinion @1 festivals for 3 : The drums at the feast go right through your chest. I'd give anything to be the one beating them.
opinion @1 city for 2 : Every arch in this city has its own voice. A newer town wouldn't have half as many to listen to.
opinion @1 watch mixed 1 : The Watch shout a lot. I'm sure they mean well. I just wish they'd mean it more quietly.
opinion @1 drink mixed 1 : Taverns are too loud for me. One cup in a quiet corner, maybe, and then home.
opinion @1 newcomers for 1 : New folk are welcome. I'll be too shy to say so, but they are.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. Oh. Sorry, you made me jump. | #greet#. I'm not much of a talker, mind.
line @2 greet [here.time=dawn] : #greet#. Early. Everything's still quiet. I like it. | #greet#. You're up before the carts.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. | #greet#. #laugh#. Hello.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : #greet#. Oh, it's you. Good. | #greet#. I was hoping I'd see you.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. | #farewell#. Mind the loud streets.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#. | Bye, then. Go #softly#.
line @1 react.news : Oh. Go on. | Really? Tell me, slowly.
line @1 react.news.new : Oh! I'd not heard. #oath#. | That's new. I'm glad you told me first.
line @1 react.news.doubt : #doubt#. It sounds too loud to be true. | I'm not sure. Somebody's made it bigger in the telling.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : Oh, no. #pity#. | That's awful. I'm so sorry.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : Oh, lovely! #laugh#. | #gladnews#. That's made my day.
line @1 answer.how : All right. A bit jumpy, as ever. | #fine#. Nothing's banged yet.
line @1 decline : #hedge#, I'd rather not. I'm hopeless in a crowd, and I'd let you down. | Sorry, I can't. There's an evening at home I've been saving, and I need it.
line @1 accept_decline : That's all right. Truly. | #no_matter.capitalize#. Another time, maybe.
line @1 thank : #thanks#. Really. | Oh, that's kind. Thank you.
line @1 preclose : Well. I'd better go before it gets loud out. | #preclose#. I'll let you get on.
line @1 accept_preclose : Go on. It was nice, this. | Bye, then. Go carefully.
line @1 tease [pair.band=friends] : You walk like a cart with a loose wheel. I can hear you three streets off. | You laugh like a goose in a cupboard. I love it.
line @1 tease.return : #laugh#. That's fair. I'll take it. | Oh, you. I'll get you back. Quietly.
line @1 ack : #laugh#. | #bc_i_know#
scene clap_under_arch
when topic=pastimes|day here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : I clapped under #arch# on my way here. It answered twice. | Every arch in the city sounds different. I've clapped under most of them. | Don't laugh. I clap under arches. #clap.capitalize#. To hear it come back.
b : Twice? | Different how? | Why?
a : Twice, then a little one, like a sneeze. That's the best arch for it. | Some ring, some thud, and one by the river laughs. Honestly. | I like being answered. Even by #stones#. #laugh#.
b? : #bc_ha# | #bc_go_on# | #bc_fair_enough#

scene jumped_again
when topic=smalltalk|day here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / react.self / laugh
a : #bang.capitalize# behind me just now. #jumped.capitalize#. | Somebody dropped a pan in the next room and I was halfway up the wall. | I jump at everything. Doors, carts, my own sneezes.
b : Are you all right? | Halfway up the wall? | Your own sneezes?
a : Fine. My heart's still going, that's all. #laugh#. | Clinging on. Then I laughed so hard I had to sit down. | Especially those. They come out of nowhere.

scene the_big_drum
when topic=dreams|festival
does confide / react.self / assess
a : I want to beat #drum# at the feast. The biggest one. In front of everyone. | You'd not think it, quiet as I am. But I want to be the loudest thing in the procession. | One day I'll carry #drum#. I've told nobody. Well, you now.
b : That's a big wish. | The loudest? You? | Your secret's safe.
a : It is. I'll get there. Slowly. Quietly. #laugh#. | Me. Funny, isn't it? I'll still jump at the first beat. | Thank you. Don't laugh if you see me practising.

scene table_drumming
when topic=pastimes|home self.homeless!=yes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I practise #tapping#. The neighbours are very patient. | I've worn a dip in the table with two spoons. | I can do the feast beat now. All of it. On a pot lid.
b : Very patient? | A dip! | All of it?
a : Mostly. One knocked on the wall. In time, mind. | Two spoons and three years. It's a good dip. | All of it. The end's the hard part. I miss it every time.

scene night_lane
when topic=day|weather here.time=night
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : At night you can hear the river from #lane#. Right through the city. | I like the city at night. Every little sound has room to be heard. | Somebody was whistling three streets off just now. I could hear every note.
b : I never noticed. | Little sounds? | Every note?
a : Stand still a moment. There. | A cat on a roof. A tap dripping. A shutter. Lovely. | Every one. Slightly out of tune. #laugh#.

scene snow_hush
when topic=weather|season here.weather=snow
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : Snow eats all the echoes. I clapped under #arch# and nothing came back. | Listen. Nothing. The whole city's gone soft. | I love snow. Nothing makes a sudden bang in snow.
b : Nothing at all? | It's so quiet. | Nothing?
a : A little thud. Like the stones were sleepy. | It is. I could stand in it all day. | Not a thing. Even the carts creep about.

scene thunder_jump
when topic=weather here.weather=storm
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Thunder. I'll be under the table if anyone wants me. | Every clap of thunder, I jump. Every single one. | It's only noise. I know that. My legs don't.
b : It can't hurt you. | Every one? | Your legs?
a : I know. I'll come out when it's finished. #laugh#. | Every one. You'd think I'd learn. | My legs have never listened to me. Not once.

scene procession_drums
when topic=festival|season
does tell.feeling / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : When the drums come down the street at the feast, I feel them in my teeth. | I follow the drummers the whole way round. I don't care who sees. | I can tell you every drummer by their beat. The third one's always early.
b : In your teeth? | The whole way round? | Always early?
a : In my teeth, my ribs, everywhere. Nothing else feels like it. | The whole way. My feet are sore the next day. Worth it. | Always. Half a beat. Nobody else notices.
b? : #bc_lovely# | #bc_ha# | #bc_ha#

scene apple_cake
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : There's #cake# in my pocket. It's for later. It's getting squashed. | The baker on the corner does #cake# on Marketday. I'm always first. Quietly first. | I'd trade a good supper for #cake#. Don't tell my stomach.
b : Squashed cake's still cake. | Quietly first? | I won't tell.
a : So I keep reminding it. | I stand very still by the door so nobody notices me. Then I'm first. | Thank you. #laugh#. It's a secret between us.

scene work_rhythm
when topic=work self.working=yes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I work to a beat. It goes quicker. One, two, and lift. | Don't mind me humming. It's a drum part. In my head. | I work quietly. Folk forget I'm here. Then I sneeze and they jump.
b : Does it help? | A drum part? | And then?
a : It does. I'm the quickest when I've a good beat. | The feast beat. I'm practising without the drum. | Then I laugh, and they laugh. It's nice.

scene shouting_street
when topic=quarrel|crime|smalltalk
does tell.worry / reassure / assess
a : Somebody was shouting in the street. I stayed in till it stopped. | I can't bear shouting. It goes right through me. | There was a row on the corner. I took the long road round, by #lane#.
b : It's over now. | Nor me. | Sensible.
a : I know. My ears are still ringing. | I'm all right now. Just a bit shaky. | Took me ages. Still, the long way has the better arch.

scene teasing_echo
when topic=friends|smalltalk pair.band=friends
does tease / tease.return / laugh
a : You clap too loud. You frighten the arches. | I heard you sing at the feast. #laugh#. The arch did too. | You sneak up on folk. I'm sure you do it on purpose.
b : The arches can take it. | And what did the arch think? | Only on you. You jump so nicely.
a : They can, but can I? #laugh#. | It sang back. Out of tune, mind. Like you. | You're terrible. I'm glad of you.

story the_laughing_arch [topic=memories|lore self.age>=18]
  : There's an arch down by the river. Years ago, I clapped under it and it laughed back. A proper laugh.
  : My fur stood straight up. Then I laughed, and it laughed again. It was me all along, of course.
  ask : Would you have run?
  b : I'd have run, and not stopped till home.
  b[old] : I know that arch. It laughed at me once too.
  : I nearly did. Now I go back on purpose.

story first_drum [topic=memories|festival self.age>=20]
  : At my first feast, a drummer let me hit the big drum. Just once.
  : It was so loud I sat down in the road. Everyone laughed. I didn't mind. I wanted to do it again.
  ask : Did you ever want something that frightened you a bit?
  b : All the time. The fright tells you it matters.
  b[old] : Most of what I've ever wanted, now I think of it.
  : There, you see. That's the drum for me.

rule @arch_bark
when concept=bark here.region=ridgemere here.time=day|dusk
does aside
cooldown 8h
say #clap.capitalize#. There. It answered. | #oath#. That one rings lovely.

rule @bang_bark
when concept=bark here.weather=storm
does aside
cooldown 10h
say Oh! Oh. Only thunder. #laugh#. | #jumped.capitalize#. Again.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. Oh, sorry, you startled me. What is it? | #greet#. I'm not much of a talker. But ask.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #greet#, #topic.player#. Back again. I'm pleased. | #topic.player#. Oh, good. A face I know.
dlg @3 resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : Oh. Please don't shout. Say it quietly and I'll do what I can. | #greet#. You look cross. I'd rather we were quiet about it.
dlg @1 resident.job : I work. To a beat, mostly. It goes quicker that way. | Work. And drumming, when nobody's listening.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. Clap under an arch for me. | #farewell#. Go #softly#.
graft resident.hub
choice Why did you just clap under that arch? -> arch_clap
node arch_clap
say To hear it answer. Every arch sounds different. Some ring, some thud. One by the river laughs. I like to be answered, even by stones.
mood warm
free
choice Which one is the best? -> arch_best
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node arch_best
say The old one by the steps. It answers twice, then a little one like a sneeze. Try it. Softly, though. It's shy, like me.
choice I'll try it. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye


young
line @1 greet : #greet#. You made me jump. #laugh#. | #greet#. I'm listening to the arch.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. | #greet#. #laugh#. Hi.
line @1 farewell.return : Bye. Clap for me. | Bye bye. Go quiet.
line @1 react.news : Oh. Truly? Slowly, please. | Really? I didn't know that.
line @1 answer.how : All right. A cart banged and I jumped. | Good. I found a new echo.
line @1 decline : Not there, please. It's ever so loud, and I'll get frightened. | No, thank you. I'm shy today. Very shy.
line @1 accept_decline : All right. Thank you for asking me. | That's fine. I'll stay here.
scene pup_echo_game
when topic=pastimes|friends here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : We played echoes under #arch#. I clapped and everybody shouted back. | If you say your name under #arch#, it says it back. Twice. | I found an echo by the steps nobody knows about. Only me.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : That's a fine game. | It does, doesn't it. | A secret echo? Lucky.
b : Who won? | Twice? | Can I hear it?
a@grown : It's the best game. | Once loud, once small. | Very lucky. I'm keeping it.
a : The arch. It always wins. | Twice. The second's like a whisper. | Maybe. If you're quiet.

scene pup_big_bang
when topic=smalltalk|day
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A cart dropped all its barrels and I jumped right up a step. | The door slammed and I hid behind the water butt. Then I laughed. | Somebody popped a bag behind me. I squeaked.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : Barrels make a fearsome noise. | Behind the water butt? Good spot. | Squeaked! Poor thing.
b : Did you fall? | Then you laughed? | Squeaked?
a@grown : They do. My ears hurt. | It's my best spot. | I'm all right now. #laugh#.
a : No. I just went up. Like a cat. | Because it was only a door. | A little squeak. Like a mouse.

scene pup_pot_drum
when topic=family|pastimes self.mother
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I play drums on the pots. #self.mother# says one pot only. | #self.mother# took me to see the drummers. I didn't jump once. Nearly once. | I'm going to be a drummer. #self.mother# says start small.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : One pot is plenty. | Nearly once is well done. | Small's how everybody starts.
b : Only one? | Not once? | Start small?
a@grown : One pot is too small. | It was a very big drum. | I'm small. So that's all right.
a : One. I make it count. | Nearly. A big one made me. | A small drum. Then a big one.

scene pup_shy_lessons
when topic=day|smalltalk self.stage=young
does tell.feeling / reassure / assess
a : I had to say a thing in front of everybody today. I went all hot. | When people look at me I forget my words. | Somebody laughed when I said the wrong word. I wanted to hide.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : Everybody goes hot. You'll grow out of it. | Your words come back, though. | They laughed at the word, not at you.
b : Did you say it? | All of them? | I'd have hidden.
a@grown : I hope so. Soon. | They do. Later. In bed. | Oh. I didn't think of that.
a : Yes. Very quietly. | All of them. Then they came back. | I nearly did. Then I laughed too.

scene pup_snow_quiet
when topic=weather|season here.weather=snow
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : When it snows, our street hushes right down. I love it. | I clapped in the snow and nothing came back. Where did it go? | Snow is the best. Nothing goes bang.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : Snow swallows sound. | The snow ate it. | Nothing at all, for once.
b : Very quiet. | Where? | Nothing?
a@grown : I like that it does. | Greedy snow. #laugh#. | For once. It's lovely.
a : Like everybody's asleep. | The snow ate it, I think. | Not even carts. They're too slow.

story pup_arch_name [topic=memories|pastimes self.stage=young]
  : I whispered my name under the old arch, and it whispered it back.
  : So now the arch knows me. I say hello every time I go past.
  b[stage=adult|old] : That's a good friend to have. Does it say hello back?
  b : Does it say hello back?
  : Only if I say it first. That's manners.

rule @pup_clap_bark
when concept=bark here.region=ridgemere
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Clap! Listen. It answered! | Echo! Echo! #laugh#.

dlg @5 resident.hub : #greet#. You made me jump. #laugh#. What is it? | #greet#. Shh. I'm listening to the arch.

adolescent
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. Sorry, I'm a bit jumpy. | #greet#. Oh. Hello.
line @1 farewell.return : Bye. Go quietly. | See you. #laugh#.
line @1 react.news : Oh. Go on, slowly. | Really? Who said?
line @1 answer.how : All right. Practising. Always practising. | Fine. Still jumpy. Getting better.
line @1 decline : I'd rather not. It's crowded, and I'll just stand in a corner. | Sorry, no. I've drum practice, and I'm behind.
scene teen_asked_drummers
when topic=dreams|festival self.stage=adolescent
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I asked the feast drummers if I could learn. Out loud. Me. | The drummers said come back when I can keep the beat. I can keep the beat. | I practise the feast beat every night. On the bedpost now.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : That took nerve. Good for you. | Then go back and show them. | On the bedpost? Brave bedpost.
b : What did they say? | Can you? | Every night?
a@grown : I shook the whole time. But I asked. | I will. When I've stopped shaking. | It's a very patient bedpost. #laugh#.
a : Maybe next year. That's not no. | Nearly always. Nearly. | Every night. The end's still hard.

scene teen_voice_small
when topic=smalltalk|friends self.stage=adolescent
does tell.feeling / reassure / assess
a : Everybody my age shouts. I can't. My voice just won't go big. | Somebody said I'm too quiet to be any fun. #laugh#. I'm fun. Quietly. | I'm always the one nobody hears in a crowd.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : A quiet voice gets listened to. | Quiet fun's the best kind. | The ones worth hearing do hear you.
b : Does it matter? | You are fun. | I hear you.
a@grown : I hope so. It gets ignored, mostly. | That's what I said. Sort of. | That's kind. I'll try to remember.
a : A bit. Not much. I've got the drum for loud. | Thank you. #laugh#. | Good. That's enough, then.

scene teen_arch_map
when topic=pastimes|day self.stage=adolescent here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I've clapped under every arch between the chapel and the Wharf. Forty-two. | I've a favourite arch for every mood. A thud one for cross days. | I took a friend to the laughing arch. They screamed. Then they laughed.
b[stage=adult|old] #grown : Forty-two! That's a lot of clapping. | A thud for cross days. That's wise. | The laughing arch? Which one's that?
b : Forty-two? | A thud one? | They screamed?
a@grown : Forty-two. And a doubtful one. | It helps. Thud, and done. | By the river. I'll show you sometime.
a : I counted twice to be sure. | Low and dull. It's very soothing. | Then laughed. That's what the arch is for.

rule @teen_beat_bark
when concept=bark here.region=ridgemere
does aside
cooldown 8h
say One, two, and three. Feast beat. | #clap.capitalize#. Forty-three, maybe.

dlg @4 resident.hub : #greet#. Sorry, I'm not good at talking. Ask, though. I'll try.
